Subject: url: on OpenVMS, report an unsupported file-name conversion only with -d

convert_fname() converts each file name from the remote encoding (UTF-8)
to the locale's code set with iconv().  The VSI C RTL's iconv() has only
the converters installed under SYS$I18N_ICONV, often none, and the C
locale's code set is "ASCII", so every download printed "Conversion from
'UTF-8' to 'ASCII' isn't supported".  The name is used unchanged, as
before; on VMS the message is now debug output.

--- a/src/url.c	2026-10-04 08:07:56.359847064 +0100
+++ b/src/url.c	2026-10-04 08:07:56.393669590 +0100
@@ -1616,8 +1616,16 @@
   cd = iconv_open (to_encoding, from_encoding);
   if (cd == (iconv_t) (-1))
     {
+#ifdef __VMS
+      /* The C RTL's iconv() has only the converters installed under
+         SYS$I18N_ICONV (often none), and the C locale's code set is
+         "ASCII", so this fails for every download; say so only with -d.  */
+      DEBUGP (("Conversion from %s to %s isn't supported\n",
+               quote_n (0, from_encoding), quote_n (1, to_encoding)));
+#else
       logprintf (LOG_VERBOSE, _ ("Conversion from %s to %s isn't supported\n"),
                  quote_n (0, from_encoding), quote_n (1, to_encoding));
+#endif
       return fname;
     }
 
